  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3423": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Concord University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor of Computer Science Skip to Main Content Directory | MyCU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Concord University Home Human Resources Chamber of Commerce of the Two Virginias Employment Notices Adjunct Instructor of Computer Science Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Concord University is a public liberal arts institution with an enrollment of approximately 2,000 students. Nestled in the scenic mountains of southern West Virginia, our campus offers access to year-round outdoor recreation, a close-knit community, and a supportive academic environment. We encourage applications from women, minorities, people with disabilities, and veterans. Requirements for Completed Application: Cover Letter addressing teaching philosophy CV Unofficial copy of transcripts (The selected candidate will be required to submit official copies of transcripts before time of appointment Three references and their contact information (including a current address, phone number and e-mail address) Selected candidates for the position will be asked to first participate in a phone or zoom interview. Candidates selected from this interview will then be invited to campus. This visit will include a teaching demonstration by the candidate. The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science has seven full-time faculty. Five Mathematics faculty teach General Education courses and service courses to the University. Two Computer Science faculty teach approximately 85 undergraduate students pursing degree options in Computer Science, Computer Information Systems, Cybersecurity, and Data Analytics. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Job Category Hourly/Adjunct Position Title Adjunct Instructor of Computer Science Working Title Adjunct Instructor of Computer Science Scheduled Hours Per Week FLSA Status Job Summary Job Summary The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science at Concord University invites applications for adjunct faculty in Computer Science. We are building a pool of instructors to teach on an as-needed basis. We welcome applications from experienced educators and working professionals alike. The department offers four computing degree programs: Computer Science, Computer Information Systems, Cybersecurity, and Data Analytics. Adjuncts may teach courses across these programs. Our greatest needs are typically in foundational courses such as introductory programming, data structures, networking, and database systems. We also welcome candidates with strengths in data analytics, cybersecurity, or web and mobile application development. Courses may be offered in person on our main campus in Athens, WV, and/or online, depending on departmental needs. Online courses are a mix of synchronous and asynchronous delivery, and candidates who live outside the region are welcome to apply for online sections. Classes are small, typically 15–20 students, and teaching here is hands-on and student-focused. Successful candidates will be committed to high-quality undergraduate instruction and to helping students build a strong foundation in computing. They will also support Concord University’s mission of fostering academic excellence in a supportive learning environment. In your cover letter, please indicate whether you are interested in teaching in person, online, or both. Duties and Responsibilities Duty/Responsibility To perform this job successfully, an individual must: Design and facilitate learning experiences that enable student success and achieve student learning outcomes. Develop expectations and assess student learning outcomes. Assess student learning through assignments, tests, and other evaluations, grading fairly and consistently, and providing timely feedback to support student progress. Maintain regular office hours to provide academic support, assist with course-related questions, and contribute to student recruitment and retention efforts. Other duties as assigned by the Department Chair or Dean. % of Time 100% Education/Knowledge Minimum Education Master's Required Licenses/Certification Applicants must hold at least a master’s degree in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Data Analytics, or a closely related field. College-level teaching experience is preferred, and relevant industry experience will also be considered. Required Skills Strong teaching and communication skills, with the ability to explain concepts clearly to a wide range of learners Ability to create a supportive and engaging learning environment Skilled in developing instructional materials and using effective teaching strategies Proficiency with learning management systems and basic instructional technology Strong organizational abilities, including timely grading, accurate record-keeping, and adherence to academic policies Ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students · Commitment to Concord University’s mission and a strong commitment to, and understanding of, the role of CS education. Required Experience Type of experience Needed Strong teaching and communication skills, with the ability to explain concepts clearly to a wide range of learners Amount of Experience Needed (Months/Years) More than 5 years Posting Detail Information Close Date Open Until Filled No Additional Information Concord University is a public liberal arts institution with an enrollment of approximately 2,000 students. Nestled in the scenic mountains of southern West Virginia, our campus offers access to year-round outdoor recreation, a close-knit community, and a supportive academic environment. We encourage applications from women, minorities, people with disabilities, and veterans. Requirements for Completed Application: Cover Letter addressing teaching philosophy CV Unofficial copy of transcripts (The selected candidate will be required to submit official copies of transcripts before time of appointment Three references and their contact information (including a current address, phone number and e-mail address) Selected candidates for the position will be asked to first participate in a phone or zoom interview. Candidates selected from this interview will then be invited to campus. This visit will include a teaching demonstration by the candidate. The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science has seven full-time faculty. Five Mathematics faculty teach General Education courses and service courses to the University. Two Computer Science faculty teach approximately 85 undergraduate students pursing degree options in Computer Science, Computer Information Systems, Cybersecurity, and Data Analytics. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.concord.edu/postings/3422 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Optional Documents Concord University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Concord University 1000 Vermillion Street P.O. Box 1000 Athens, West Virginia 24712-1000 1-800-344-6679 | 1-304-384-3115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
